# Common timebase support
# This is intended for use by animations, not for simulation times. It is strongly recommended
# for implementations to update this value at ~1 Hz.
# `last` must be finite and non-decreasing during one main-channel session.
# Clients reset their offset estimate when a new session begins.

# Implementations should maintain a local clock. When this component is updated, compute:
#   tA = TimeSyncComponent.last
#   tL = local_now_at_receive
# Then compute an offset estimate:
#   offset_est = tA - tL
# Maintain a smoothed offset (EWMA):
#   offset = lerp(offset, offset_est, alpha) where alpha ranges between 0.02–0.1 depending on update rate.
# Then compute “estimated authority time now” locally as:
#   auth_now_est = local_now + offset
# The exposed estimate must not move backward. If an offset update would cause a
# reversal, clients converge gradually while preserving monotonic output.

pack TimeSyncComponent
- last : f64 # authority monotonic seconds at send time
